From: OTB R4 Development <otb-r4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 13:05:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: net: realtek: document layer3+4 LAG hash opt-in

The RTL930x has two global trunk distribution masks. Document an opt-in
property for boards which reserve mask 1 for source/destination IP and L4
ports instead of the default layer2+3 tuple.

This lets the DSA driver advertise only the hash policy actually programmed
in hardware and keeps the existing behaviour on all other boards.

Signed-off-by: OTB R4 Development <otb-r4@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../bindings/net/realtek,rtl9301-switch.yaml      | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/realtek,rtl9301-switch.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/net/realtek,rtl9301-switch.yaml
@@ -44,6 +44,14 @@ properties:
   ethernet-ports:
     type: object
 
+  realtek,lag-hash-layer3-4:
+    type: boolean
+    description:
+      Reserve trunk distribution mask 1 for source and destination IP
+      addresses plus source and destination layer 4 ports. When enabled,
+      the DSA driver accepts layer2 or layer3+4 bonding policies instead of
+      the default layer2 or layer2+3 policies.
+
 patternProperties:
   'reboot@[0-9a-f]+$':
     $ref: /schemas/power/reset/syscon-reboot.yaml#
